===Etymology===
{{etymon|en|:inh|enm:blak|tree=1}}
From {{inh|en|enm|blak}}, {{m|enm|black}}, {{m|enm|blake}}, from {{inh|en|ang|blæc||black, dark", ''also'' "ink}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*blak}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*blakaz||burnt}}, possibly from {{inh|en|ine-pro|*bʰleg-||to burn, shine}}.

See also {{cog|nl|blaken||to burn}}, {{cog|nds|blak, black||blackness, black paint, (black) ink}},<ref>https://www.koeblergerhard.de/mnd/mnd_b.html</ref> {{cog|goh|blah||black}}; also compare {{cog|la|flagro|flagrāre|to burn}}, {{cog|grc|φλόξ|t=flame}}, {{cog|sa|भर्ग||radiance}}.

{{senseno|en|sullen|uc=1}} is a {{sl|en|yue|黑面|nocap=1|tr=hak1 min6|t=to pull a long face, to scowl}}.

